# Secrets / generated PKI material — never commit
# Anchored: a bare `pki/` also matches (and hides) the tracked scripts/pki/ sources.
/pki/
# Backstop for private keys that land outside /pki/ (the runbooks in docs/ write
# device.key.pem etc. into the cwd); the trailing * covers .new / .expired copies.
*.key.pem*
*.csr.pem
# Scratch files from the first-enrollment walkthrough in docs/operations.md
# (cookies.txt is a live admin session).
/cookies.txt
/enroll*.json
/device.cert.pem

# Build artifacts
/bin/
/out/
*.raucb
*.raucb.meta.json
device/health/atomic-health
device/health/*.o
# `go build ./cmd/...` without -o drops the binary into the module dir
/server/atomic-server
/device/agent/atomic-agent

# Yocto / kas (device/meta-atomic/README.md; CI sets KAS_WORK_DIR to ./build)
/build/
/device/meta-atomic/build/
# kas clones each layer repo into its work dir, named by the repo key
poky/
meta-openembedded/
meta-raspberrypi/
meta-rauc/
meta-rauc-community/
# externalsrc puts these symlinks into the source dirs it points at
# (device/agent, device/health); symlinks, so no trailing slash
oe-workdir
oe-logs
*.wic
*.wic.bmap
*.ext4

# CI outputs / caches, left behind when the jobs' commands are run locally
/.cache/
/staging-sha256.txt
/publish-manifest.json
/e2e/logs/

# Node / UI
node_modules/
server/ui/dist/
# vite empties this dir on every build. index.html stays trackable so that
# `//go:embed all:dist` still has a file to embed on a fresh clone.
server/internal/web/dist/*
!server/internal/web/dist/.gitkeep
!server/internal/web/dist/index.html
# vite leaves its bundled config behind if it crashes (package.json is type: module)
server/ui/vite.config.*.timestamp-*

# Go
*.test
coverage.out
coverage-func.txt

# Local env / config
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
/device/agent/agent.conf
compose.override.y*ml

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
